      "question": "If SPRING is coded as 79 and MAGIC is coded as 102, then how will LEAST be coded?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "text": "76"
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "text": "77"
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "text": "78"
        },
        {
          "label": "4",
          "text": "79"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "3",
      "solution": "The pattern follows here is,\n\nTake Z = 1, Y = 2, X = 3 ........ A = 26\n\nSPRING = S (8) + P (11) + R (9) + I (18) + N (13) + G (20)\n\n= 8 + 11 + 9 + 18 + 13 + 20\n\n= 79\n\nMAGIC = M (14) + A (26) + G (20) + I (18) + C (24)\n\n= 14 + 26 + 20 + 18 + 24\n\n= 102\n\nSimilarly,\n\nLEAST = L (15) + E (22) + A (26) + S (8) + T (7)\n\n= 15 + 22 + 26 + 8 + 7\n\n= 78\n\nHence, LEAST will be coded as** 78.**",
      "tags": [
        "Coding Decoding Based on Numbers"
      ]
