          "label": "4",
          "text": "28%"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "1",
      "solution": "Given, \n\nCost price of 15 chains = Rs.7,520\n\nSelling price of 15 chains = Rs.9,450\n\nTherefore, Profit = Selling price - Cost price\n\n= 9,450 - 7,520\n\n= 1930\n\nWe know, Profit % = (profit/cost price) ×100\n\nProfit % = (1930/7520) × 100 = **25.664 ≈ 26 %**\n\nHence, **option 1** is the correct answer.",
      "tags": [
        "Quant Based Puzzle"
      ]
